# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Studio (Vite) — only VITE_* variables reach the browser.
#
# Copy to `.env`. Every one of these is optional; the studio works with none
# of them set. The relay's own PORT/HOST live in `server/.env` instead — this
# file is read by Vite at build time and never by the Node server.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the signaling relay lives. Leave unset to resolve automatically:
# ws://<host>:3001 during development, the page's own origin when deployed
# behind a proxy. Set it when the relay is hosted somewhere else.
# VITE_SIGNALING_URL=wss://signal.example.com

# TURN relay, for connections that STUN alone cannot traverse — symmetric NAT
# and firewalls that block UDP. Without one, two peers on such networks gather
# candidates, fail every connectivity check, and the studio reports `failed`.
# This is the single most common cause of "connection failed".
#
# Comma-separated. Credentials can be shared across all of them (below) or
# appended per URL as turn:host:port|username:password.
# VITE_TURN_URLS=turn:turn.example.com:3478,turns:turn.example.com:5349
# VITE_TURN_USERNAME=
# VITE_TURN_CREDENTIAL=
